  "curriculum": "UvA Biomedical Sciences, RIO 56990, is the Dutch-language, full-time 180 EC bachelor. Its first two years are compulsory. Use the 2026–2027 curriculum PDF for the 3 EC biomedical data science course, which the live HTML lists with a dash. First year is 60 EC, second year is 60 EC, and the selected third year is 30 EC Frontiers in Medical Biology, 12 EC open electives and an 18 EC project. Frontiers comprises 12 and 6 EC taught blocks, 6 EC experimental genomics and 6 EC restricted choice. Keep the 6 and 12 EC slots open. The extended 30 EC project replaces the 12 EC elective block and is a distinct route, as are a minor or exchange in place of specialisation. Frontiers extends the general molecular and experimental identity more broadly than the nervous-system or clinically oriented options.",
  "progression": "The official year-one programme moves from cells, genetics, microbes and statistics to anatomy, physiology and disease. The year-two laboratory sequence combines biochemistry and cell biology with molecular techniques and immunology, before microscopy, genome analysis and the mini-thesis. The dated diagram places the Frontiers and genomics modules in the first semester of year three before electives and the project. The current study page describes independent research in a placement and an English report. The UvA accreditation report for ISAT 56990 records completion of the first two years before the research placement. The regular 60+60 EC preceding sequence meets that threshold. The accreditation report is corroboration for progression only. Use the 2026–2027 sources for module identities and credits.",
